---
// The article beside "On this page" (specs/docs-site-chrome.md). Overrides Starlight's
// TwoColumnContent (~0.40), whose right rail is `position: fixed` at the top of the viewport and full
// height — under our PageFrame that would cover the site header and footer. Here it is a plain grid
// inside the page column: from 72rem (Starlight's own ToC breakpoint, fixed in its PageSidebar) the
// rail is a sticky second column; below, the rail holds Starlight's "On this page" dropdown, sticky at
// the top of the viewport above the article. Styles are in src/styles/docs.css (`.hipo-two-col`).
---

<div class='hipo-two-col'>
  {
    Astro.locals.starlightRoute.toc && (
      <aside class='hipo-toc print:hidden'>
        <slot name='right-sidebar' />
      </aside>
    )
  }
  <div class='main-pane min-w-0'><slot /></div>
</div>
